contentText:
GIRLSET discusses new single “Tweak,” working with Missy Elliott and the group&#8217;s iconic covers of classic pop songs.

Tetris Kelly: This is Tetris hanging out with GIRLSET talking about this single that&#8217;s about to come, &#8220;Tweak.&#8221; How are you doing, ladies?

GIRLSET: Good!&nbsp;

OK, I gotta say, starting the track right away with the SWV sample. I was already ready to get in there, so tell me how you arrived at using that sample in kind of this word play with &#8220;Tweak&#8221; and &#8220;Weak.&#8221;

Camila Ribeaux Valdes: I mean, I think we didn&#8217;t really know that the sample was going to be used, but when we first heard the song, it was like, obviously the intro of the song, and that was like-&nbsp;

Savanna Collins: Really catching, yeah. Like, immediately.&nbsp;

Camila Ribeaux Valdes: Did not expect that, but we&#8217;re like, &#8220;No way that&#8217;s like, so iconic.&#8221; So I feel like it&#8217;s really an honor to be able to have a little bit of that iconic song in our song, and it kind of sets the tone, I feel like for &#8220;Tweak,&#8221; it&#8217;s like a twist. &#8220;Weak&#8221; and &#8220;Tweak,&#8221; it&#8217;s kind of like the opposite, I would say, in terms of like meaning, it really ties in together.

And talk about the meaning of the song. I mean, you guys obviously recently re-debuted. So tell me about the sound you wanted to create and what the meaning of the song is.&nbsp;

Lexus Vang: Yeah. I mean, it&#8217;s really about like standing your ground, as we say, a stupid boy anthem, someone who keeps pushing your boundaries, your limits. It&#8217;s also an emotional song, but maybe in the opposite way. And we loved enhancing the emotional aspect, but in a way where it&#8217;s kind of like standing on business, but also being real with yourself. Being real with yourself, keeping yourself in check. And like, the title says &#8220;Tweak.&#8221;&nbsp;

Keep watching for more!
